<title>GERMANY: Mannesmann Mobilfunk sees 1996 profit rise.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann Mobilfunk sees 1996 profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mannesmann Mobilfunk GmbH said it expects 1996 sales to total 4.2 billion marks, up from 2.7 billion last year, and a parallel increase in profit.</p>
<p>The Mannesmann AG unit's D2 mobile phone network had 2.3 million customers in December, up from a reported 2.2 million in October.  </p>
<p>In 1995, Mannesmann Mobilfunk showed a profit of 464 million marks. The net increase in D2 subscribers this year totaled 850,000, it said.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
